An unbind that settles a waiting lender but not the borrower it lends to.
The borrower keeps the queue the lender's old account gave it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread names a queue it is not for

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -455,7 +455,7 @@ void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
     }
     *bound = (struct cap){ 0 };
     /* A thread without units holds nothing, so settling empties its account as it takes the thread off its queue. */
-    lender_settle(t);
+    thread_settle(t);
 }
 
